<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beidi Commandery</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Beidi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/commandery">Commandery</a>, the 'Northern Land', was a commandery of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> and Han empires on the north-western frontier of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu">Gansu</a> and Ningxia. It was created by the state of Qin after it destroyed the Yiqu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rong-people">Rong</a> in the 3rd century BCE and guarded the frontier against the steppe peoples.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>He sent tribute to Cao Cao and later dealt with the rival Three Kingdoms, and in 231 he marched to <b>Beidi</b> in support of Zhuge Liang's northern campaign against Cao Wei.</blockquote><a href="/empire/xianbei">Xianbei · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Qin annexed his lands, created the Longxi, <b>Beidi</b> and Shang commanderies and built a long wall to protect them.</blockquote><a href="/state/yiqu">Yiqu</a></li></ul></section>
